    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d778">

                <pb facs="0874" n="782" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg782"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/11434</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-09-23T14:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 23, 1918, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5694. For Jassy:</p>
                <p>In reply to your joint telegram dated September 14, you may assure Roumanian
                    Government and people that purpose of the Government and people of the United
                    States has not been modified in any way and remains as expressed in message from
                    the President telegraphed to you November 1 [<hi rendition="#italic">28</hi>],
                        1917.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d778-f1"/> You may reiterate the sense of that
                    message emphatically.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
